**Convention 6.3 (credited repair outside both restricted arguments).**
[GDB, Theorem 23.1][GDB] permits arbitrary proper syndrome-row
subsets in (WBF.28), rather than only forests, and evaluates their
parity-symmetrized sums by rank. It proves the attained optimum

$$
U_{\rm rank}=2n+(n-1)\log_2
                  \frac{A^{n/(n-1)}+B^{n/(n-1)}}2,
\qquad 0\le U_{\rm rank}-\log_2 Z_G\le1.
\tag{WBF.32}
$$

That supplied result uses the equal mixture of all one-row deletions
and the actual common syndrome. It is a repair of this sector and is
not a rule in Definition 2.1. Its availability prevents interpreting
Theorem 5.2 as an impossibility of obtaining small loss on this
carrier by richer methods. Proposition 6.2 only shows that the
existing forest excess does not itself evaluate the Finner class;
it is not a general ordering of the two methods on all instances.

